## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a safe, production-grade debugging workflow leveraging Time Travel and dbt macros while preserving tenant isolation and clear rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped debug mirroring
- dbt macros for environment toggling
- Snowflake Time Travel for backfills
- CI gating and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```sql
{% macro swap_tenant_debug(tenant, mode) -%}
  {% if mode == 'debug' -%}
  create or replace view analytics_{{tenant}}.hourly_engagement as
  select * from analytics_{{tenant}}.debug_hourly_engagement;
  {% else -%}
  create or replace view analytics_{{tenant}}.hourly_engagement as
  select * from analytics_base.hourly_engagement;
  {% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you safely expire old debug objects?
- How would you audit backfill changes across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design registry-driven per-tenant masking, consistent lineage, and CI across tenants, while handling late data and schema drift.

## Key Concepts

- Macro-based per-tenant masking
- Dynamic per-tenant schemas from a registry
- Schema drift guards and late data handling
- Global lineage tracking and cross-tenant isolation in CI

## Code Example

```javascript
// simplified macro skeleton
{% macro mask_for_tenant(field, tenant) -%}
  {% if tenant in var('full_access_tenants') -%}
    {{ field }}
  {% else -%}
    sha256({{ field }})
  {% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test masking correctness across tenants in CI?
- How would you handle a tenant revocation of access mid-cycle?
